  {
    "id": "how",
    "title": "Hope without prophecy",
    "labels": [
      "Possibility",
      "Agency",
      "Fellowship"
    ],
    "lines": [
      "Here hope is not prediction; it is commitment to a possible good under uncertainty.",
      "It asks whether an outcome is possible, valuable and influenceable enough to justify action.",
      "Awe widens the horizon, agency finds a lever, and fellowship makes effort endurable."
    ],
    "emotionalPlan": {
      "arc": "From a precise redefinition through a practical test to the human mechanics that sustain effort.",
      "purpose": "Show how the book rebuilds hope as a disciplined, non-naive stance.",
      "states": [
        "clarity",
        "analytical focus",
        "gathering energy"
      ],
      "intensities": [
        0.5,
        0.45,
        0.6
      ],
      "voiceDirections": [
        "Precise and calm, separate 'prediction' from 'commitment'.",
        "Measured, give each of the three criteria its own beat.",
        "Building warmth across the three clauses, natural pace."
      ]
    },
