  {
    "id": "what",
    "title": "Reality has seams",
    "labels": [
      "Frontiers",
      "Survivable failure",
      "First step"
    ],
    "lines": [
      "Its frontiers run from an unmapped mind to a universe that is still mostly night.",
      "Courage becomes rational when institutions make intelligent failure survivable.",
      "Read it for a hope that survives tragedy because it never promised an ending.",
      "Begin with the prologue, We Are Too Early to Give Up, and choose a frontier."
    ],
    "emotionalPlan": {
      "arc": "Wonder at the open frontiers grounds itself in institutions, then settles into a personal, quiet invitation.",
      "purpose": "Present selected content, give a specific reason to read and a real starting point.",
      "states": [
        "wonder",
        "grounded conviction",
        "earnest warmth",
        "quiet invitation"
      ],
      "intensities": [
        0.65,
        0.5,
        0.55,
        0.35
      ],
      "voiceDirections": [
        "Expansive and unhurried, a slight lift on 'mostly night'.",
        "Firm and practical, stress 'survivable'.",
        "Sincere and personal, slower on the final clause.",
        "Soft and direct, say the prologue title as a title."
      ]
    },
    "chapter": "03 · Reality has seams",
